    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483-a3">

                <pb facs="0653" n="547" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg547"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dawson to the
                            minister of foreign affairs of the Dominican
                            Republic.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-01-12"><hi rendition="#italic">January 12,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: Confirming my note of yesterday, I
                    have the honor to inform you that the names of the three individuals in asylum
                    at my legation are: Carlos F. Morales, President of the Republic; Enrique
                    Jiminez, and Gregorio <pb facs="0654" n="548" xml:id="pg548"/> Encarnacion.
                    These gentlemen ask that passports be granted them to go to San Juan, P. R. In
                    case these passports are given to them the commander of the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dubuque</hi> is disposed to carry them to their
                    destination.</p>
                <p>I shall be grateful if you will kindly take the necessary steps as soon as
                    possible.</p>
                <p>I improve, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. C. Dawson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
